#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:60
msgid "Enter your readings, then choose Calculate. Nothing is submitted or saved by this calculator."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:61
msgid "Inputs changed. Calculate again to update the result."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:62
msgid "Enter a number for each measurement. Use a decimal point or decimal comma, without grouping separators or scientific notation."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:63
msgid "All fabric lengths and the opening length must be greater than zero."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:64
msgid "Offsets and the conversion length must be zero or greater."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:65
msgid "Stretched length cannot be less than original length. Check the marked points and units."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:66
msgid "Use a whole number from 2 to 100 for the number of button centres."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:67
msgid "The two offsets together must be less than the opening length."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:68
msgid "These values exceed a reliable numerical range. Recheck the measurements and use a suitable unit."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:69
msgid "Choose centimetres, millimetres or inches."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:70
msgid "Check your readings: "
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:71
msgid "Stretch"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:72
msgid "Residual change after release"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:73
msgid "Recovered extension"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:74
msgid "Not defined: the stretched reading equals the original reading."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:75
msgid "The released reading is outside the original-to-stretched range. The signed results are shown without clamping. Remeasure the sample; this arithmetic does not diagnose fabric behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:76
msgid "A negative residual change means the released reading is shorter than the original. Recovery is a percentage of the stretched extension, not of the original length."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:77
msgid "Interval between centres"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:78
msgid "Centre positions measured from the top"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:79
msgid "Converted length"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:80
msgid "Results display up to six decimal places. Keep full readings; round only when marking with your ruler."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:106
msgid "Sewing measurement calculators"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:107
msgid "Arithmetic for your own readings. Use the same unit and the same marked points within each fabric test. A decimal point or decimal comma is accepted; do not use thousands separators."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:118
msgid "Measurement-method reference from Sewlore"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:120
msgid "Enable JavaScript for the interactive results. The formulas and worked examples above remain available."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:142
msgid "Centimetres (cm)"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:143
msgid "Millimetres (mm)"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:144
msgid "Inches (in)"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:153
msgid "Calculate"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:162
msgid "Fabric stretch and recovery"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:163
msgid "Record one marked direction before stretching, while stretched, and after release. These readings do not determine suitable garment ease or replace a fabric test."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:165
msgid "Original length"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:166
msgid "Stretched length"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:167
msgid "Released length"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:168
#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:190
msgid "Unit for all three lengths"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:171
msgid "Formulas and hypothetical example"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:172
msgid "Stretch = 100 × (stretched − original) ÷ original. Residual change = 100 × (released − original) ÷ original. Recovered extension = 100 × (stretched − released) ÷ (stretched − original)."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:173
msgid "For original 10 cm, stretched 14 cm and released 10.5 cm: stretch is 40%, residual change is 5%, and recovered extension is 87.5%. No sample was measured for this example."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:183
msgid "Button-centre intervals"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:184
msgid "Offsets locate the first centre from the top and the last centre from the bottom. Use 2–100 centres. Check closure instructions, seam allowances and buttonhole sizes before marking."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:186
msgid "Opening length"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:187
msgid "First centre: offset from top"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:188
msgid "Last centre: offset from bottom"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:189
msgid "Number of centres"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:193
msgid "Formula and hypothetical example"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:194
msgid "Interval = (opening length − top offset − bottom offset) ÷ (number of centres − 1). Position i = top offset + i × interval, with i starting at zero."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:195
msgid "A 60 cm opening, 3 cm offsets at both ends and 7 centres give six 9 cm intervals. Positions from the top are 3, 12, 21, 30, 39, 48 and 57 cm. No garment was tested for this example."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:205
msgid "Length unit conversion"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:206
msgid "Enter a non-negative length. This converter changes the unit; the unit menus in the other tools only label the readings you enter."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:208
msgid "Length to convert"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:209
msgid "From unit"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:210
msgid "To unit"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:213
msgid "Conversion definitions"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:214
msgid "1 cm = 10 mm. 1 international inch = exactly 25.4 mm. For example, 2.54 cm converts to 1 in. Conversion does not improve measurement precision."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:222
#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:232
msgid "Sewing Calculators"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:233
msgid "Add a Shortcode block to a post or page, then paste:"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:235
msgid "Choose a single tool with tool=\"stretch\", tool=\"buttons\" or tool=\"units\". The default shows all three."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:236
msgid "Optional external reference link"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:237
msgid "The calculator displays no external link by default. Only add show_reference=\"yes\" if you want a public link to the Sewlore measurement-method guide. Removing the link does not change any calculation."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:239
msgid "Read the measurement-method guide"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:240
msgid "Privacy and limits"
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:241
msgid "Calculations run in the visitor’s browser using assets served by this site. The plugin has no telemetry, forms that submit data, cookies, storage, account requirement, external runtime or background requests. Clicking an optional reference link visits that external site."
msgstr ""

#: sewlore-sewing-calculators.php:242
msgid "These tools calculate arithmetic from user readings. They do not measure fabrics, select garment ease, diagnose fit or guarantee closure performance. Check the relevant pattern and test a sample."
msgstr ""
